  "name": "Example: Expressing an Inequality as a Union of Intervals",
  "problem": "Express the compound inequality $x < 4$ or $x \\ge 10$ using interval notation.",
  "worked_solution": "We can represent the compound inequality on a number line, as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14191664/assets/26594fb87ed7eca0803d554e4a1fbd3d3719cc01ba4e70f96126b73924ac5769.png)\n\nThis number line consists of the interval $(-\\infty, 4)$ as well as the interval $[10, \\infty).$\n\nSo, we can express the compound inequality as the union of these two intervals:\n\n$$\n(-\\infty, 4) \\:{\\cup}\\: [10, \\infty)\n$$",
